---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/okad-house.css';
---

<Base title="OKAD vs Billo: UGC Video Production Compared (2026)" description="OKAD agency vs Billo platform — full comparison for brands choosing UGC video production. Strategy, quality, pricing, and creator management.">
  <div class="okh">

    <section class="khero" style="padding: 80px 0 48px">
      <div class="w" style="max-width:900px">
        <span class="kick">OKAD vs Billo</span>
        <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.2rem);margin-bottom:16px">OKAD vs Billo — <span class="cap">Which Is Right for You?</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">One is a done-for-you agency with strategy built in. The other is a self-serve marketplace for quick UGC clips. Here's the honest comparison to help you decide.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px">
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);margin-bottom:16px">Side-by-side comparison</h2>
      <div style="overflow-x:auto">
        <table class="cmp-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th></th>
              <th>OKAD</th>
              <th>Billo</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Type</td>
              <td class="highlight">Full-service agency</td>
              <td>Self-serve platform</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Strategy</td>
              <td class="highlight">Included (scripts, hooks, angles)</td>
              <td>DIY — you write the brief</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Creator Quality</td>
              <td class="highlight">600+ vetted creators</td>
              <td>Open marketplace</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Price</td>
              <td class="highlight">From $500 / 10 videos</td>
              <td>$59–$159 per video</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Scripts</td>
              <td class="highlight">Written by the team</td>
              <td>Templates provided</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Editing</td>
              <td class="highlight">Done-for-you (pro editing)</td>
              <td>Basic editing only</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Testing</td>
              <td class="highlight">Framework included</td>
              <td>None</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px">
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);margin-bottom:16px">When OKAD is better</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:16px">Choose OKAD when you need strategy, production, and testing handled by one team. You don't have to write briefs, manage creators, or figure out what to test — that's the whole point.</p>
      <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:24px;display:grid;gap:10px;color:var(--soft, #4d4d49)">
        <li>You want someone to own the creative strategy, not just shoot clips.</li>
        <li>You need professional editing — cuts, captions, pacing, music.</li>
        <li>You're running paid ads and need a testing framework to find winners.</li>
        <li>You want a team that learns what works for your brand over time.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px">
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);margin-bottom:16px">When Billo is better</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:16px">Billo works well when you already know exactly what you want, can write your own briefs, and just need someone to record the footage.</p>
      <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:24px;display:grid;gap:10px;color:var(--soft, #4d4d49)">
        <li>You need a quick, one-off UGC clip and have the brief ready.</li>
        <li>Your budget is under $500 and you only need 1–3 videos.</li>
        <li>You have an in-house editor and just need raw creator footage.</li>
        <li>You're comfortable managing the creative process yourself.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px">
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem);margin-bottom:24px">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Is OKAD more expensive than Billo?</summary>
          <p>Not per video. OKAD's batch pricing starts at $500 for 10 videos ($50/video), which is cheaper than Billo's $59–$159 per video. The difference is that OKAD includes strategy, scripting, and professional editing — Billo gives you the raw clip.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need to manage creators with OKAD?</summary>
          <p>No. OKAD handles creator selection, briefing, communication, and quality control. With Billo, you browse the marketplace, select creators, write the brief, and manage revisions yourself.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I use Billo for paid ads?</summary>
          <p>You can, but Billo doesn't include ad strategy or performance testing. You'll get raw UGC clips that you'll need to edit, caption, and test on your own. OKAD delivers ad-ready videos with a testing framework built in.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Which is better for scaling ad creative?</summary>
          <p>OKAD. Scaling requires systematic testing — different hooks, angles, creators, and formats. OKAD's model is designed for this: produce a batch, test on real spend, identify winners, and iterate. Billo is a one-video-at-a-time marketplace without a testing layer.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="background:var(--stage, #111);padding:80px 24px;text-align:center">
      <div style="max-width:700px;margin:0 auto">
        <h2 style="color:#fff;font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.2rem);margin-bottom:16px">Ready to test?</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--stage-soft, #8e8e8e);margin-bottom:32px">Get 10 UGC video ads with strategy, scripting, and editing included. See results in under a week.</p>
        <a class="btn dew" href="https://calendly.com/okad_calls/first" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Book a free strategy call</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is OKAD more expensive than Billo?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not per video. OKAD's batch pricing starts at $500 for 10 videos ($50/video), which is cheaper than Billo's $59–$159 per video. The difference is that OKAD includes strategy, scripting, and professional editing — Billo gives you the raw clip."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need to manage creators with OKAD?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. OKAD handles creator selection, briefing, communication, and quality control. With Billo, you browse the marketplace, select creators, write the brief, and manage revisions yourself."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I use Billo for paid ads?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "You can, but Billo doesn't include ad strategy or performance testing. You'll get raw UGC clips that you'll need to edit, caption, and test on your own. OKAD delivers ad-ready videos with a testing framework built in."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which is better for scaling ad creative?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "OKAD. Scaling requires systematic testing — different hooks, angles, creators, and formats. OKAD's model is designed for this: produce a batch, test on real spend, identify winners, and iterate. Billo is a one-video-at-a-time marketplace without a testing layer."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>

  <style>
    .cmp-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 32px 0; }
    .cmp-table th, .cmp-table td { padding: 16px 20px; text-align: left; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule, #e6e6e6); font-size: 15px; }
    .cmp-table th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink, #111); background: var(--card, #f2f2f2); }
    .cmp-table td:first-child { font-weight: 500; color: var(--soft, #8e8e8e); width: 140px; }
    .cmp-table .highlight { background: #f4f9e8; }
    .faq-list { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
    .faq-list details { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule, #e6e6e6); padding-bottom: 12px; }
    .faq-list summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.05rem; padding: 8px 0; color: var(--ink, #111); }
    .faq-list details p { padding: 8px 0 4px; color: var(--soft, #4d4d49); line-height: 1.6; }
  </style>
</Base>
